{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788112556440775001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"camlet-exodermal-kodiakbear","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"58b00f530adfead352a068b1a110cc0edc0aa33d454b5cd93494ce11e370bf85","event_uuid":"cd1d31ed-18ab-4fb0-a066-9b0ed0ae621d","position":{"commit_sha":"f57bb6d9d7636288b0f20d3e45262c7086cf8023","position":"1788112416761629942-cd1d31ed-18ab-4fb0-a066-9b0ed0ae621d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"114ba458d2f2411c74ea8e8109715e6ac53be6f8899052abf69b83f5fb5781b1","event_uuid":"2e9fdfe3-fa4a-40fb-9125-9dd50ea6cb30","position":{"commit_sha":"92e335deb22c92bbd6c4002aba006d24d141775d","position":"1788112556440775000-2e9fdfe3-fa4a-40fb-9125-9dd50ea6cb30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788112416761629942,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2e9fdfe3-fa4a-40fb-9125-9dd50ea6cb30","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"96f9-e324-c22f-49a2"}],"description":"## Problem\n`workflow/steps.py::GATE_POLICIES` (`default`/`strict`/`advisory`) fails a workflow step by\nexact string membership of `finding[\"severity\"]` in a fixed list (e.g. `[\"critical\", \"high\"]`\nfor `default`). This is the same impact-only signal the epic is retiring, and since\n`severity` is derived from impact alone while the real BLOCK decision already uses\n`priority = validity x impact >= block_threshold`, the two gates can disagree on the exact\nmotivating bug: a high-impact/low-validity finding trips `fail_on_severity` while `priority`\nsays it should not block.\n\n## Approach\nReplace each policy's `fail_on_severity: [...]` list with a `priority_threshold: float | None`\n(`None` means never fails, matching today's `advisory` policy):\n- `default`: reuse `review_kernel.decide.DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD` (the same single source of\n  truth `pass3_decide` uses for its own BLOCK decision) rather than a second hardcoded number.\n- `strict`: a lower threshold than `default` (catches more) -- `DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD` minus\n  a fixed documented margin, so it stays strictly stricter than `default` without a second\n  magic constant.\n- `advisory`: `priority_threshold: None` (never fails), matching today's empty\n  `fail_on_severity: []`.\nUpdate the `gate` step (`steps.py:215-239`) to compare\n`finding.get(\"priority\", 0.0) >= policy[\"priority_threshold\"]` instead of the severity\nmembership test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GATE_POLICIES` in `workflow/steps.py` has no `fail_on_severity` key remaining; each\n  policy has a `priority_threshold` key (`float` or `None`).\n- [ ] The `default` policy's threshold equals `review_kernel.decide.DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD`\n  (imported, not duplicated as a literal).\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_steps.py` passes with `test_gate_fails_on_high_severity`,\n  `test_gate_strict_fails_on_any_finding`, `test_gate_advisory_never_fails`, and\n  `test_gate_unknown_policy_falls_back_to_default` rewritten to construct findings with a\n  `priority` value instead of a `severity` string, asserting the same pass/fail behavior for\n  equivalent priority values.\n- [ ] A new test proves the config-effect contrast: the same finding (fixed priority) gates\n  differently under `default` vs `strict` vs `advisory`, run through the real `gate` step.\n\n## Testing\nTier: in-process unit test against the real `gate` workflow step function. Oracle: the\nstep's returned pass/fail verdict for a finding of a given priority, under each named policy.\nConfig-effect contrast (test-design.md sec.6): run the same finding through `default` and\n`strict` and assert the outcomes differ where priority sits between the two thresholds.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","96f9-e324-c22f-49a2"],["parent","c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fc84-a6a6-14c3-4bc8","ticket_type":"task","title":"Migrate fail_on_severity workflow gate to a priority threshold","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cd1d31ed-18ab-4fb0-a066-9b0ed0ae621d","2e9fdfe3-fa4a-40fb-9125-9dd50ea6cb30"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788112556440775001,"uuid":"af69c4d2-eac5-4944-a736-e91608af4851"}